How can I utilize the LanguageTool API in Java to check for grammatical errors in a sentence? For instance, if I have the sentence "I loves to dance", how can I use the API to detect the error and suggest a correction?
Here is an example Java code that utilizes the LanguageTool API to accomplish this task:
import java.io.IOException;
import org.languagetool.JLanguageTool;
import org.languagetool.language.AmericanEnglish;
public class GrammarChecker {
 public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
 JLanguageTool langTool = new JLanguageTool(new AmericanEnglish());
 String sentence = "I loves to dance";
 List matches = langTool.check(sentence);
 for (RuleMatch match : matches) {
 System.out.println("Potential error at characters " + match.getFromPos() +
 "-" + match.getToPos() + ": " + match.getMessage());
 System.out.println("Suggested correction: " + match.getSuggestedReplacements());
 }
 }
}
With this code, you can easily identify grammatical errors in a given sentence and suggest possible corrections.
